---
import Skelet from "../layouts/Skelet.astro";
import Gradient from "../components/Gradient.astro";
import CardCategory from "../components/Card_Category.astro";
import "../style/styles.css";
---

<Skelet>
  <main>
    <section>
      <Gradient />
      <div class="image_section"></div>
    </section>
    <div class="headline_section">
      <div class="categories">
        <CardCategory className="program" text="Talk" />
        <CardCategory className="program" text="Branding" />
        <CardCategory />
      </div>
      <h1>Designing Brands in a Noisy World</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="details_grid">
      <p>Date: 04.09.2025</p>
      <p>Venue: BLOX</p>
      <p>Time: 12:00-13:00</p>
      <p>Speaker: Sara Coleman</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about_grid">
      <div class="about_left">
        <h3>( About )</h3>
        <p>
          In today’s crowded digital space, creating a brand that stands out is
          more challenging than ever. In this talk, Sara Coleman, a creative
          director at Coleman & Co. Branding (Berlin), delves into strategies
          for cutting through the noise. Using real-world examples from global
          campaigns, Sara will explore how to develop a strong visual identity
          and a compelling narrative that resonates with audiences. Whether
          you're working with a startup or a global brand, this session will
          help you craft a brand identity that speaks clearly and powerfully.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sara will also share insights from her recent collaborations with
          leading sports apparel brands in the skiing and skateboarding scenes.
          Known for building bold, youthful brand identities, she has crafted
          campaigns that fuse high-energy photography with playful,
          community-driven storytelling—think snapshots from après-ski parties,
          dynamic quotes from pro snowboarders, and eye-catching imagery of
          tricks on the slopes. These projects have resonated strongly with
          younger audiences, gaining traction across social media and coming to
          life at branded events like DJ-led pop-ups and interactive showcases.
          It’s branding that feels alive, authentic, and unmistakably
          of-the-moment.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <img />
        <p class="image_text">
          Sara Coleman, with 15+ years of experience in branding, has led
          projects for clients such as Adidas, Volkswagen, and Carhart.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h3>( Discover More from Sara Coleman )</h3>
    <div class="socials_flexbox">
      <div class="socials_flex">
        <p>Instagram</p>
        <a>@sara_colemancreative</a>
      </div>
      <div class="socials_flex">
        <p>LinkedIn</p>
        <a>Sara Coleman/LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
      <div class="socials_flex">
        <p>Website</p>
        <a>www.saracolemancreative.com</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Skelet>

<style>
  main {
    margin: 60px 0px;
  }
  h3,
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    margin-left: 20px;
    margin-right: 20px;
  }
  h3 {
    margin-top: 50px;
  }
  p {
    margin: 0px 20px;
  }
  .categories {
    display: flex;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .socials_flexbox {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    width: 100%;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--Black, #060604);
  }
  .socials_flex {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--Black, #060604);
    padding-top: 15px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
  }
  .details_grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr;
  }
  .details_grid p {
    padding: 15px 0px;
  }
</style>
